{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0F4M", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-ctf}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6ca3d8a21f3e1fb33d3374a8bca0f23518659556994cdbfe962465e64d94724b", "source_text": "Tor finite with constructible cohomology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7308eb912e2cd0e494627ab60944927538c82eac9e82d22870d3b9895e4edacc", "unit_id": "tag:0F4M:title"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0F4M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$D_c(X_\\etale, \\Lambda)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-Dc}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:22ccc31f4ecf0b16b4169a2761f8ad65e9cc351549c9233e13986c6f2e27dea0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c2127712a51e9f11466a601dc4374d01a104b42c60c45be35f7b2470d75ca5d7", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme and let <MATH_0002> be a Noetherian ring. An often used\nsubcategory of the derived category <MATH_0003> defined\nin Section <REF_0001> is the full subcategory consisting of objects\nhaving (locally) finite tor dimension. Here is the formal definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:76ff3096ab70366266322c345589e94b306e956ee6f48e8e57e24d4d51880ac0", "unit_id": "tag:0F4M:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0F4M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$D_{ctf}(X_\\etale, \\Lambda)$", "MATH_0004": "$D_c(X_\\etale, \\Lambda)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-ctf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f4323b5c2789794bf75d2db5ef0fd3abc213117a546cfecafa153b89597cf93b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a1452530012e10faa07204b0dfe30bddfdcd02ee2541d5d6429a321accf8f990", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a Noetherian ring. We denote\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> the full subcategory of\n<MATH_0004>\nconsisting of objects having locally finite tor dimension.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:df996f341f4c7ffdbdccd3629a9090c65003fa020ce681261a803d54ae85a6a9", "unit_id": "tag:03TQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0F4M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$D_c(X_\\etale, \\Lambda)$", "MATH_0002": "$D(X_\\etale, \\Lambda)$", "MATH_0003": "$$\nD_{ctf}(X_\\etale, \\Lambda) \\subset D^b_c(X_\\etale, \\Lambda)\n\\subset D^b(X_\\etale, \\Lambda)\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$D_{ctf}(X_\\etale, \\Lambda)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-cohomology-definition-tor-amplitude}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-when-ctf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e549a8c6db03be626abf87c785668048477f11fde31e885b7181fe88d6f74f18", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e51021eac97f26966a97b4ba7179f5ab57f3ad5c7c64b9dc27dd1595e6ff0002", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is a strictly full, saturated triangulated subcategory of\n<MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002>. By our conventions, see\nCohomology on Sites, Definition <REF_0001>,\nwe see that\n<MATH_0003>\nif <MATH_0004> is quasi-compact. A good way to think about objects of\n<MATH_0005> is given in Lemma <REF_0002>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:10ced12c1e5c886e164a01fff7a7e9961141bb17ca0bebd480289a7a1126f9db", "unit_id": "tag:0F4M:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "0F4M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$D_{ctf}(X_\\etale, \\Lambda)$", "MATH_0002": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_X)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0006": "$D_{ctf}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-different}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:92edf2c07e100a452243e6b7382e2f7a3856db45d1878217233247ffa7d3f932", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b9d9a5786a2432c0ed3ca9450e918bb871078ae16e1cad6dba4ca3304d210520", "source_text": "Objects in the derived category <MATH_0001> in some sense have\nbetter global properties than the perfect objects in  <MATH_0002>.\nNamely, it can happen that a complex of <MATH_0003>-modules\nis locally quasi-isomorphic to a finite complex of finite locally free\n<MATH_0004>-modules, without being\nglobally quasi-isomorphic to a bounded complex of locally free\n<MATH_0005>-modules. The following lemma shows this does not\nhappen for <MATH_0006> on a Noetherian scheme.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e59549631b43012c08be38c6efab34994d287fc1a2aa4dc254c5f34751653d2c", "unit_id": "tag:03TS:statement"}
